[\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"CHINA BLACKLISTS MP MATERIALS AND USA RARE EARTH — BEIJING ADDS 10 US FIRMS TO EXPORT CONTROL LIST AS CRITICAL MINERALS WAR ESCALATES\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-06-22/china-places-two-us-rare-earths-producers-on-export-control-list\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Bloomberg\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"rare-earths\",\n    \"snippet\": \"China's Ministry of Commerce added MP Materials Corp. (NYSE: MP) and USA Rare Earth Inc. (Nasdaq: USAR) — the two US rare earth producers most heavily backed by the US government to reduce Chinese dependence — to its export control list on June 22, 2026, barring Chinese companies from exporting 'dual-use' items to both firms as retaliation for Washington's expansion of its own military-linked entity list; China added 10 American companies in total. While market analysts note the curbs are partly symbolic because both MP Materials and USA Rare Earth have already substantially reduced their reliance on Chinese-origin equipment and materials, the listings carry significant strategic signal value: China is formally designating the US producers it considers the most dangerous to its rare earth processing monopoly, validating precisely the thesis that drove $5B+ in federal investments into domestic rare earth supply chains since 2024. For retail investors, the listing paradoxically acted as a catalyst for both stocks — the Motley Fool reported on June 23 that shares of MP and USAR rose on the news, as the market interpreted the ban as confirmation that US producers are now close enough to operational independence that China felt compelled to escalate.\",\n    \"is_featured\": true,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"KLDC MIRADO STEPS OUT 120m SOUTH — 79.63 g/t AU OVER 2.1m CONFIRMS HIGH-GRADE SYSTEM EXTENDING BEYOND KNOWN ABITIBI RESOURCE, SECOND DRILL ADDED\",\n    \"url\": \"https://investingnews.com/kirkland-lake-discoveries-extends-mirado-system-120-m-south-step-out-hits-79-63-g-t-au-over-2-1-m-100-m-west-step-out-intersects-0-98-g-t-au-over-62-3-m/\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Investing News Network / Kirkland Lake Discoveries Corp. (TSXV: KLDC)\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"exploration-discovery\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Kirkland Lake Discoveries Corp. (TSXV: KLDC) reported June 23, 2026 that drillhole KLM26-010 — the southernmost hole in the program — was collared approximately 120 metres south of previously known Mirado Project mineralization and returned 79.63 g/t Au over 2.1 metres (including 184.04 g/t Au over 0.8m) along with a second high-grade interval of 53.46 g/t Au over 1.4 metres; a 100-metre west step-out hole (KLM26-011) simultaneously intersected a broad 0.98 g/t Au over 62.3 metres, extending the envelope of the South Zone mineralized system to the southwest and down-dip. Over 10,000 metres of the 25,000-metre 2026 drill program are now complete, visual results consistently confirm a large fluid-rich mineralizing system, and a second diamond drill from Chibougamau Drilling is now turning at the property — the first time Mirado has had two rigs active simultaneously. With the Mirado property located 20 km southeast of Kirkland Lake in Ontario's Abitibi gold belt, the 120-metre south step-out result structurally extends the South Zone beyond all previously modeled boundaries, establishing the geometry for a system that is larger than initially defined and which will require a substantially expanded drill program to constrain.\",\n    \"is_featured\": true,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"MAGNA MINING LEVACK HITS 29.7% COPPER EQUIVALENT OVER 3.4m — 9.4% CU, 19.8 g/t AU, 8.8 g/t PT+PD AS NICU GRADUATES FROM TSXV TO TSX\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/06/22/3315139/0/en/Magna-Mining-Intersects-29-7-Copper-Equivalent-over-3-4-metres-consisting-of-9-4-Copper-2-3-Nickel-19-8-g-t-Gold-and-8-8-g-t-Platinum-Palladium-within-the-R2-Footwall-Zone-at-the-L.html\",\n    \"source_name\": \"GlobeNewswire / Magna Mining Inc. (TSX: NICU)\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"copper-base-metals\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Magna Mining Inc. (now trading TSX: NICU after graduating from the TSXV effective June 23, 2026) announced June 22 that drilling has intersected 29.7% copper equivalent over 3.4 metres within the R2 Footwall Zone at the Levack Mine in Sudbury, Ontario — comprising 9.4% copper, 2.3% nickel, 19.8 g/t gold, and 8.8 g/t combined platinum and palladium — among the highest grade-thickness intercepts recorded at the project to date. Two surface rigs and one underground rig are currently active at Levack with a fourth drill mobilizing in late June, all targeting the R2 Footwall Zone's massive sulphide veins ahead of a Preliminary Economic Assessment expected in Q3 2026 and a restart decision in H2 2026. The simultaneous TSX graduation signals that Magna has met the more rigorous listing standards of the senior exchange — a milestone that typically broadens institutional access and improves trading liquidity for previously TSXV-listed producers. For retail investors tracking Sudbury battery-metals producers, R2 Footwall intercepts of this grade at a mine scheduled for PEA completion this quarter represent the clearest pre-production drill catalyst of 2026 in the Sudbury district.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"GUINEA BANS RAW GOLD EXPORTS — AFRICA'S 6TH-LARGEST PRODUCER ORDERS LOCAL REFINING AS CONAKRY REFINERY NEARS COMPLETION\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.mining.com/web/guineas-president-announces-ban-on-raw-gold-exports/\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Mining.com\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"gold-silver\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Guinean President Mamadi Doumbouya announced a ban on raw gold exports on June 21-22, 2026, requiring all gold produced in Guinea — Africa's sixth-largest gold producer — to be refined domestically into ingots before export, with operators who continue to export unrefined gold facing immediate license suspension and termination of their mining agreements. The Nimba Gold Refinery in Conakry is near completion with a rated capacity of approximately 250 tonnes per year, which Doumbouya cited as the logistical foundation for enforcing the new requirement. Guinea's industrial gold sector is dominated by foreign-owned mines, and the ban creates an immediate compliance challenge for operators without domestic refining arrangements, potentially disrupting near-term concentrate and dore shipment schedules. The move reflects a broader continental trend of gold-producing nations seeking to capture more value-added revenue domestically — a structural shift that increases operational risk for junior explorers and mid-tier producers with Guinea assets who had planned to export ore or dore offshore for toll processing.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"COPPER GIANT MOCOA: 1,052m CONTINUOUS MINERALIZATION BELOW PIT — THIRD BRECCIA CORRIDOR CONFIRMED AT COLOMBIA PORPHYRY AS PEA ADVANCES\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.juniorminingnetwork.com/junior-miner-news/press-releases/2126-tsx-venture/cgnt/205895-copper-giant-extends-mineralization-below-the-conceptual-pit-at-mocoa-and-confirms-a-third-mineralized-corridor.html\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Junior Mining Network / Copper Giant Resources Corp. (TSXV: CGNT)\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"copper-base-metals\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Copper Giant Resources Corp. (TSXV: CGNT) announced June 22, 2026 that deep infill hole MD-064 at its flagship Mocoa copper-molybdenum porphyry project in Putumayo, Colombia intersected 1,052 metres of continuous mineralization — including 486 metres averaging 0.57% copper equivalent (0.41% Cu and 0.029% Mo) that exceeds the current Mineral Resource Estimate average of 0.51% CuEq — while directional daughter hole MD-063 delivered the first modern confirmation of a western breccia corridor, establishing a third drill-tested mineralized breccia zone at Mocoa and supporting interpretation of a multi-phase porphyry system with multiple mineralized centers. MD-063 also extended continuous mineralization below the current conceptual pit through ground previously modeled as waste, confirming the system continues at depth and to the south toward the La Estrella discovery corridor where a third rig is conducting maiden drilling. With three rigs now active across Mocoa-La Estrella and a PEA advancing, the confirmation of a third breccia corridor increases the optionality for the resource estimate update and reinforces the thesis that Mocoa is one of the largest undeveloped copper porphyry systems in the Americas.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"ALAMOS GOLD ISLAND DISTRICT REVEALS 67.93 g/t OVER 3.05m AND NEW 250m WEST EXTENSION — $43M DRILL PROGRAM UNLOCKS MULTIPLE FEED SOURCES\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.mining.com/alamos-logs-multiple-high-grade-hits-at-island-gold\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Mining.com / Alamos Gold Inc. (TSX: AGI)\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"exploration-discovery\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Alamos Gold Inc. (TSX: AGI) released June 22, 2026 multi-target underground and surface drilling results from the Island Gold District in northern Ontario confirming a new Island West Extension Zone approximately 250 metres west of existing underground Mineral Reserves, with hole MX26-031 returning 5.2 metres at 12.05 g/t Au from approximately 968 metres depth, MX26-035W cutting 5.6 metres at 8.07 g/t Au from 928 metres, and a separate Cline-Pick target returning 3.05 metres at 67.93 g/t Au. Alamos has budgeted $43 million for 2026 Island Gold District exploration — up from $24 million in 2025 — targeting 50,000 metres of underground drilling to add Mineral Reserves and Resources near existing workings ahead of the expanded Magino mill ramp-up. The Island West Extension discovery at 250 metres from the reserve boundary suggests the Island Gold orebody remains open in a direction that was previously under-explored, and the high-grade Cline-Pick intercept introduces a potential new source of higher-grade mill feed that could materially improve the blended head grade of the combined Island-Magino operation.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"CHINA IMPORTED 163 TONNES OF GOLD IN MAY — HIGHEST SINCE MARCH 2024 AS DOMESTIC DEMAND RUNS 76% ABOVE PRIOR-YEAR LEVELS\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.mining.com/web/chinas-gold-imports-surge-to-most-in-more-than-two-years/\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Mining.com / Bloomberg\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"gold-silver\",\n    \"snippet\": \"China imported approximately 163 tonnes of gold in May 2026 — the highest monthly volume since March 2024 — bringing total imports for the January-to-May period to approximately 692 tonnes, a 76% increase versus the same period in 2025, according to Bloomberg data reported June 22, 2026. Hong Kong gold bar imports also surged ahead of the mainland clearing system launch, suggesting a pre-positioning effect from large institutional buyers. The sustained Chinese demand volume is structurally significant for the gold market: it occurs simultaneously with the June 2026 price correction toward $4,130 — meaning Chinese buyers are actively accumulating gold precisely as Western speculative capital exits via ETF outflows. This east-west demand divergence provides a physical demand floor beneath current prices that analysts note was absent during the 2012-2014 gold bear market, when neither Chinese retail demand nor central bank purchases were large enough to offset Western institutional liquidation at scale.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"THE GOLD BUG WHO BECAME THE PRINTER IS DEAD — ALAN GREENSPAN, 100, LEAVES PRECIOUS METALS INVESTORS A COMPLICATED LEGACY\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/06/22/alan-greenspan-former-chairman-of-the-fed-dies-at-age-100.html\",\n    \"source_name\": \"CNBC / Money Metals Exchange\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"opinion-analysis\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Former Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan died June 22, 2026 at age 100, leaving gold investors with one of monetary history's great contradictions: in 1966, Greenspan wrote 'Gold and Economic Freedom' — arguably the most lucid defence of the gold standard by any mainstream American economist — arguing that the gold standard prevents government deficit spending and that 'in the absence of the gold standard, there is no way to protect savings from confiscation through inflation.' Greenspan then spent 18 years as Federal Reserve chair (1987-2006) presiding over the most expansive credit creation cycle in US history, lowering rates to 1% in 2003 and contributing directly to both the 2008 financial crisis and the 18-year gold bull market that followed. Money Metals Exchange's editorial 'RIP Alan Greenspan, Schizophrenic Gold Bug' observes that Greenspan never formally recanted his 1966 views — his 2007 memoir again advocated the gold standard — making him the rare Fed chair who both understood gold's role in preserving economic freedom and chose systematically to undermine it.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"SPARTAN METALS CONFIRMS TUNGSTEN SKARN + 1,320 ppm BERYLLIUM AT PAST-PRODUCING EAGLE MINE, NEVADA — CRITICAL MINERALS CLUSTER OPENS DRILL TARGETS\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.newsfilecorp.com/release/302423/Spartan-Metals-Exploration-Program-Confirms-Tungsten-Skarn-Discoveries-at-past-Producing-Mine-at-Eagle-Project-Nevada\",\n    \"source_name\": \"Newsfile Corp. / Spartan Metals Corp. (TSXV: W)\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"exploration-discovery\",\n    \"snippet\": \"Spartan Metals Corp. (TSXV: W) announced June 23, 2026 that its 2026 exploration program at the Eagle Tungsten-Silver-Rubidium Project in Nevada has confirmed two tungsten skarn zones at the Tungstonia Claims within the historic Eagle mine workings, with rock sampling returning tungsten assays of 0.99% to 1.87% WO3 alongside 3.3% zinc and 1,320 parts per million beryllium — a beryllium concentration not previously reported at the Eagle Project. Beryllium at 1,320 ppm is strategically significant: it is among the rarest of the US government's 50 designated Critical Minerals, with the US currently dependent on a single domestic mine for its entire supply, making any US-jurisdiction beryllium occurrence with drill-testable continuity strategically relevant well beyond its economic grade. The discovery of a skarn-hosted multi-critical-mineral assemblage of tungsten, beryllium, zinc, and silver at a historic producing mine provides Spartan with multiple commodity optionalities for a planned drilling campaign in a political environment where both tungsten and beryllium qualify for US government strategic reserve consideration.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"headline\": \"GOLDSEEK: GOLD, SILVER, COPPER BULLS SURVIVE IRAN DEAL DERAILMENT — WILD TWO-WAY MOVES EXPECTED BUT METALS TREND INTACT\",\n    \"url\": \"https://goldseek.com/article/asian-metals-market-update-22nd-june-2026\",\n    \"source_name\": \"GoldSeek (Asian Metals Market Update)\",\n    \"category_slug\": \"opinion-analysis\",\n    \"snippet\": \"GoldSeek's Asian Metals Market Update for June 22, 2026 maintains a bullish structural view on gold, silver, and copper despite the two-way price volatility triggered by the derailment of the US-Iran peace process, noting that 'wild two-way price moves are expected in gold, silver, copper, and crude oil' as the conflict timeline remains unresolved but that metal importers continue to view the overall trend as bullish. The update identifies copper as the commodity least affected by Iran-related geopolitical oscillations; the bullish copper case instead rests on a structural mine supply deficit that will likely exceed 491,000 tonnes per year through 2030 per Jefferies data. Central bank gold reserve increases — from 9% to 24% of total global reserves since 2015, recently surpassing US Treasury reserve holdings for the first time since 1996 — are flagged as the structural floor beneath the gold correction that makes the current volatility characteristically different from a primary bear market turn.\",\n    \"is_featured\": false,\n    \"is_breaking\": false\n  }\n]\n